B.OQ=new A.aS("course-L1W1-clicker-p1","**Phase 1:** Click or mark and then give the dog a treat. Repeat this until your dog has a mild startled appearance at the sound of the click/mark. This will likely be 15\u201320 times.")
B.Pk=new A.aS("course-L1W1-clicker-p2","**Phase 2:** Vary how you deliver the treat \u2014 sometimes from your hand; other times drop it on the ground after you click/mark.")
B.Wy=s([B.OQ,B.Pk],t.J)
B.O_=new A.dV("Clicker or marker conditioning","clicker","## Goal\n\nThe clicker/marker sound/word causes your dog to react by looking at you for a reward. If you don't have or are not going to use a clicker, substitute a pen click or a short word such as \"yes\" or \"good,\" and substitute your method of marking in these and future instructions. **Always follow the click or marker with food!**\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** use treats your dog identified during the Paired-Choice Preference Assessment as favorites (see your Welcome Packet).\n- **DO** attempt to keep treats off of your person when you can. Instead, keep them in a bowl on a counter, or nearby on a shelf if you are indoors.\n- **DON'T** move your hand towards the food until *after* you click.\n- **DON'T** point the clicker at the dog; it's not a remote!\n- *If your dog is afraid of the clicker, stop using it; use a pen or a marker word instead.*\n",B.Wy,null)
B.Pt=new A.aS("course-L1W1-name-p1","**Phase 1:** In a boring location, say your dog's name in a high, happy tone when you are standing near them and you can predict they will look at you. Click or mark / feed when they look at you.")
B.Pf=new A.aS("course-L1W1-name-p2",'**Phase 2:** Once they will reliably look at you when you say their name, increase the amount of time they must look at you before you click or mark / feed. Every day, wait one second longer as your dog looks at you before you click or mark / feed: *"Fluffy!" (one-thousand-one \u2014 click or mark / feed).*')
B.Pg=new A.aS("course-L1W1-name-p3","**Phase 3:** Choose a location that is slightly less boring, and repeat Phases 1 and 2. Examples might be in the back yard or on the front porch.")
B.Xr=s([B.Pt,B.Pf,B.Pg],t.J)
B.O7=new A.dV("Name recognition / attention","name","## Goal\n\nWhen you say your dog's name, they will look at you for successively longer periods of time.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** speak to your dog in a relaxed tone when you say their name.\n- **DO** say their name when you can predict they will look at you; not when they are looking at someone else or listening to a sound nearby.\n- **DON'T** lean over and stare at your dog, or use a stern tone when you say their name.\n- *We want the sound of their name to be the happy equivalent of \"We're going for a walk!\"*\n",B.Xr,null)
B.OH=new A.aS("course-L1W1-sit-p1","**Phase 1:** Use a food treat lifted backwards over your dog's head, towards their tail. *(See the Orientation video for a demo.)* When your dog sits, click or mark / feed. Do this until your dog sits every time with this hand motion / food.")
B.OL=new A.aS("course-L1W1-sit-p2",'**Phase 2:** With **NO food** in your hand, say "Sit," and make the hand motion. When your dog sits, click or mark / feed.')
B.Ow=new A.aS("course-L1W1-sit-p3","**Phase 3:** Practice in every room of the house, in the front yard, back yard, and while on walks.")
B.Xn=s([B.OH,B.OL,B.Ow],t.J)
B.NP=new A.dV("Sit","sit","## Goal\n\nWhen you say \"Sit,\" and/or make a hand signal, your dog will sit within 1 second and stay there.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** be sure to stop using the food lure as soon as is feasible. We do not want our dogs to shake us down for a treat before they sit.\n- **DON'T** push your dog's rear end down or pull them with the leash to try and force them to sit.\n",B.Xn,null)
B.Ok=new A.aS("course-L1W1-down-p1",'**Phase 1:** Have your dog sitting or standing. Touch the treat to your dog\'s nose. *(See the Orientation video for a demo.)* Say "Down." Lower the treat in a straight line to your dog\'s toes, then hold the treat on the ground. Hold the treat in place firmly, even if your dog nibbles on it. Watch her elbows. If they bend and/or touch the ground, or if the dog lies down, click or mark / feed. Then, say "Okay," and move away so your dog gets up. Do the same thing with 3\u20135 more treats. By now your dog should be putting at least their elbows on the ground when you lure them with the treat.')
B.Ph=new A.aS("course-L1W1-down-p2","**Phase 2:** Same luring technique, but do not click or mark / feed until the whole dog is down. Do this until your dog lies down quickly when you move the food lure downwards. *If your dog gets up at any time, lure them down again, but do not feed.*")
B.Po=new A.aS("course-L1W1-down-p3","**Phase 3:** Same luring technique, but do not use food, just your hand, to make the motion.")
B.Ov=new A.aS("course-L1W1-down-p4","**Phase 4:** Gradually move your hand *less* far down to make the motion.")
B.OP=new A.aS("course-L1W1-down-p5",'**Phase 5:** Say "Down" and wait for your dog to lie down before you click or mark / feed. If it takes more than one second for your dog to lie down when you say the word, go back to Phase 4. Continue to release with "Okay."')
B.Oh=new A.aS("course-L1W1-down-p6","**Phase 6:** Gradually increase the amount of time before you release the dog.")
B.Xw=s([B.Ok,B.Ph,B.Po,B.Ov,B.OP,B.Oh],t.J)
B.NZ=new A.dV("Down","down","## Goal\n\nWhen you say \"Down,\" or make the hand motion, your dog will lie down within one second and stay there.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** practice in places where your dog will not be distracted by other people, dogs, sounds or toys.\n- **DO** say \"Down\" only once each time you are training the behavior.\n- **DON'T** use your leash to pull your dog into the down position; if they aren't doing it, go to the previous phase for one session.\n",B.Xw,null)
B.Pl=new A.aS("course-L1W1-hand-target-p1","**Phase 1:** Put your flat palm close (1 inch) and parallel to your dog's muzzle. Click or mark / feed when your dog turns their head towards your hand. If they do not do so within two seconds, remove your hand and re-present. If they still do not move their head, rub a little food on your hand to entice them.")
B.Pj=new A.aS("course-L1W1-hand-target-p2",'**Phase 2:** Once your dog is reliably turning their head towards your hand, click for **deliberate bumps only**. Adding the cue, "Touch" is optional.')
B.OC=new A.aS("course-L1W1-hand-target-p3","**Phase 3:** Put your hand in different places (high, low, on floor, farther away, etc.) and use both hands.")
B.W6=s([B.Pl,B.Pj,B.OC],t.J)
B.O3=new A.dV("Hand targeting","hand-target",'## Goal\n\nWhen your dog sees your open palm, they will move towards it and touch your hand with their nose.\n\n*The actual goal of this behavior is ultimately to use your hand as a "silent" recall, or to teach tricks using hand-targeting.*\n',B.W6,u.n)
B.P6=new A.aS("course-L1W1-recall-p1",'**Phase 1:** With your dog on your regular leash, using a friendly-sounding voice, say your dog\'s name and then say "Come!" as you step back a few steps. Then: (a) click or mark as your dog moves towards you; (b) place the treat on their nose when they get to you; (c) say "Sit"; and (d) when they do, feed them the treat. *If your dog does not move towards you when you say "(Name) come!" step behind a door for 30 seconds. When you come out, have your dog sit for a few treats, then try again.*')
B.OY=new A.aS("course-L1W1-recall-p2",'**Phase 2:** Same drill, but no leash, and indoors in a boring environment. Play "Puppy Ping Pong" by calling the dog back and forth between family members. Start with everyone in the same room, calling the dog between you, then gradually make the game harder \u2014 sending people to other rooms, out of sight, up and down stairs, etc.')
B.Oz=new A.aS("course-L1W1-recall-p3","**Phase 3:** Repeat Phase 1 outside in a boring environment.")
B.Os=new A.aS("course-L1W1-recall-p4","**Phase 4:** Use a long line, repeat Phase 3 outside in a boring environment.")
B.WM=s([B.P6,B.OY,B.Oz,B.Os],t.J)
B.NO=new A.dV("Recall","recall","## Goal\n\nWhen you call your dog's name, they will run towards you and sit in front of you.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** only call your dog when you can predict they will come. If they are looking off in another direction, eating, or alerting to something more exciting than you, do not call them \u2014 you could wind up teaching them to ignore you.\n- **DO** be sure your dog is in a safe, fenced-in area when you take them off-leash. *Every year, we hear of a student dog that was hit by a car and killed. Please keep your dog safe!*\n- **DON'T** ever pull on the leash to force your dog to come.\n- **DON'T** ever offer your dog a treat to *bribe* them into coming.\n",B.WM,u.cF)
B.We=s([B.O_,B.O7,B.NP,B.NZ,B.O3,B.NO],t.e7)
B.Pz=new A.pf("Week 1",1,"We recommend doing each of the exercises below 1\u20132 times every day, if possible, for 3\u20135 minutes (it's okay to skip a day from time to time). Convenient times to fit in training can be before breakfast and dinner, during television commercials, and on quiet walks. Try to practice in at least 2\u20133 different places. If, at any time, your dog is not doing what you are asking, go back to the previous phase for a session or two.",B.We,null)
B.Pb=new A.aS("course-L1W2-name-p1","**Phase 1:** Say your dog's name when you can predict they will look at you. When they do, count *one-one thousand, two-one-thousand*, and then click or mark / feed. *If they do not look at you, move to a less distracting location.*")
B.Pr=new A.aS("course-L1W2-name-p2","**Phase 2:** Say your dog's name. Count to five as they look at you for longer periods (one one-thousand, etc.). Click or mark / feed. Do it again, count to seven. Do it again; count to four. The next time, count to eight. Vary the duration up or down 2\u20133 seconds each time, so as to be less predictable.")
B.Pm=new A.aS("course-L1W2-name-p3","**Phase 3:** Same as Phase 2, however, vary where you are in relation to the dog, and do not have any food on your person. Walk somewhere to get the food; either have it hidden in high-up containers or in another room.")
B.UH=s([B.Pb,B.Pr,B.Pm],t.J)
B.NV=new A.dV("Name recognition / attention","name",'## Goal\n\nWhen you say your dog\'s name, they will look at you for a minimum of seven seconds.\n\n## Do\'s and Don\'ts\n\n- **DO** combine practicing in "easy" (inside, no distractions) and "harder" (inside, in front of someone else, or outside) environments.\n- **DO** start in Phase 1 every week and work your way through the phases.\n- **DO** each phase five times without error before moving to the next phase.\n- **DON\'T** repeat *"Fluffy. Fluffy! FLUFFY!"* to get your dog to look at you. Say it once and then wait.\n',B.UH,null)
B.OD=new A.aS("course-L1W2-sit-p1",'**Phase 1:** Say "Sit," and make the hand motion you learned last week. When your dog sits, count *one-one-thousand*, click or mark / feed. Say "Okay," and move a little so your dog gets up. *From now on, your dog will stay sitting until you release them with "Okay."* If your dog gets up early, repeat the cue, but do not click or mark / feed when they sit. Release with "Okay."')
B.Ob=new A.aS("course-L1W2-sit-p2",'**Phase 2:** Say "Sit," and do *not* make the hand motion. If they sit, proceed as in Phase 1, adding the release after one second. If they do not sit immediately, wait one second, make the hand motion, click or mark / feed when they sit, add the release. Repeat this phase until the word "Sit" causes them to sit.')
B.OJ=new A.aS("course-L1W2-sit-p3",'**Phase 3:** Move to another room. Say "Sit." Alternate using the hand motion and the verbal cues. When the dog can do both seamlessly, increase the length of time they sit by 1\u20132 seconds before you release them.')
B.P3=new A.aS("course-L1W2-sit-p4","**Phase 4:** Same as Phase 2, more locations, longer time sitting.")
B.Yw=s([B.OD,B.Ob,B.OJ,B.P3],t.J)
B.NM=new A.dV("Sit","sit","## Goal\n\nWhen you say \"Sit,\" and/or make a hand signal, even in a distracting location, your dog will sit within one second and stay there until released.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** start with Phase 1 and work your way through the phases, going to the previous phase if your dog can't perform the task as asked.\n- **DO** vary using the verbal cue alone, the visual cue alone, and both at the same time.\n- **DON'T** hold food in your hand to get your dog to sit! If there are distractions and you need help, smear enough food on your hand to leave a scent, one time only, to help them.\n",B.Yw,null)
B.Oo=new A.aS("course-L1W2-hand-target-p1","**Phase 1:** Hold your hand next to your dog's muzzle. Click or mark / feed when they turn their head. Do each side 5x.")
B.OO=new A.aS("course-L1W2-hand-target-p2","**Phase 2:** Hold your hand one inch in front of your dog's nose. Wait. Click or mark / feed when they move their head towards your hand. Do this 10x, moving your hand \xbd inch farther away each time.")
B.P8=new A.aS("course-L1W2-hand-target-p3","**Phase 3:** Hold your hand slightly over your dog's nose, so they have to reach their head up to touch. Click or mark / feed when they do. Do this 10x, moving your hand \xbd-inch up each time.")
B.Yy=s([B.Oo,B.OO,B.P8],t.J)
B.O5=new A.dV("Hand targeting","hand-target","## Goal\n\nWhen you hold out your palm, your dog moves towards it and touches it with their nose.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** start with Phase 1 and work through the phases.\n- **DO** start in a low-distraction area and work towards more distractions.\n- **DO** make a prediction as to whether your dog will respond the way you want, *before you ask them*. If you think they might *not* do what you ask, when you ask it, **STOP**. Then work on an earlier phase.\n- **DON'T** hold your hand out for more than three seconds. If they do not touch your hand within three seconds, take your hand away, then re-present a bit closer to the dog.\n",B.Yy,u.n)
B.OS=new A.aS("course-L1W2-down-p1",'**Phase 1:** In a quiet room, say "Down," and when your dog lies down, count to five. Click or mark / feed. Do this 5x.')
B.Od=new A.aS("course-L1W2-down-p2",'**Phase 2:** Same room. As you silently count to five, pick up your foot as if you were going to move, then put it down (this is the beginning of training your dog to stay). Click or mark / feed as your dog remains in position. Release with "Okay!" Do this 10x. *Note: if your dog gets up at any time, give the cue again, but do not reward the reset. Make the next try a little easier.*')
B.P7=new A.aS("course-L1W2-down-p3","**Phase 3:** Different room. Same as Phase 1. Repeat 10x, increasing the number of seconds your dog is lying down before you click or mark / feed.")
B.Pd=new A.aS("course-L1W2-down-p4","**Phase 4:** Four different locations. Same as Phase 2 in each location.")
B.Y6=s([B.OS,B.Od,B.P7,B.Pd],t.J)
B.NX=new A.dV("Down","down","## Goal\n\nWhen you give the cue, your dog will lie down immediately and stay there until you release them. Duration of the stay can be up to 30 seconds, with you moving around the room.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** start with an easy phase and make the task harder during each session.\n- **DON'T** say the cue more than one time! If you are going to give the cue, make sure you have arranged the environment so your dog will do what you ask \u2014 study the distractions, the power of your reinforcer, and consider your previous session's success.\n",B.Y6,null)
B.OE=new A.aS("course-L1W2-recall-p1",'**Phase 1:** With your dog on the long line, in a boring-ish area, use a friendly-sounding voice, say your dog\'s name and then say "Come!" Step back a few steps. Then: (a) click as your dog moves towards you; (b) place the treat on their nose when they get to you; (c) say "Sit"; and (d) when they do, feed them the treat. Do this 5x, or for 5 minutes. *If your dog does not come the first time, use a shorter leash and/or move to a more boring location.*')
B.Ou=new A.aS("course-L1W2-recall-p2","**Phase 2:** Work on Phase 1 in 2\u20133 different safe places outdoors until your dog comes when you call.")
B.Ps=new A.aS("course-L1W2-recall-p3","**Phase 3:** Indoors, start moving to where your dog cannot see you and call them.")
B.Om=new A.aS("course-L1W2-recall-p4","**Phase 4:** *If you have a safely fenced-in yard,* drop the leash and let the dog drag it, and practice.")
B.Vi=s([B.OE,B.Ou,B.Ps,B.Om],t.J)
B.O0=new A.dV("Recall","recall","## Goal\n\nWhen you say \"Come!\" your dog will move towards you immediately, and sit in front of you when they get to you.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** use a 10- or 20-foot leash.\n- **DO** say the cue, which is \"(Dog's name), come!\" once only, in a happy-sounding tone.\n- **DO** hold onto the leash tightly, in case your dog takes off.\n- **DON'T** speak in a threatening tone, and **DON'T EVER** scold your dog for being late or for running away. *You want this phrase to sound to your dog like \"We're going for a walk!\"*\n",B.Vi,u.cF)
B.P0=new A.aS("course-L1W2-loose-leash-p1","**Phase 1:** Lure your dog to your left side with food. Ask them to sit. *(This takes some practice!)* Now, plant your dog's favorite treat on their nose, say \"Let's go!\" and start to walk. Let them nibble at the food, tiny pieces at a time, and keep the food on their nose the whole time. The idea is that the food will captivate their attention more than what is around them. *As stated above, this is only to be used occasionally, on an as-needed basis.*")
B.Oj=new A.aS("course-L1W2-loose-leash-p2","**Phase 2:** Lure your dog to your left side. With your leash and clicker in your right hand, and 3\u20134 treats in your left, say \"Let's go!\" and step off to your RIGHT, with your LEFT foot. As your dog gets up and starts to move, click or mark / feed. You will be moving to your right in a small circle, leading with your left foot each time. When your dog's head is at your knee, click or mark / feed. Gradually make the circles bigger. *Stop and take a break if you get dizzy!*")
B.Pi=new A.aS("course-L1W2-loose-leash-p3",'**Phase 3:** If your dog pulls, stop. Hold your arms against your abdomen, bend your knees, and lean back a bit if your dog is big. The idea is that the dog will *not* move forward if they pull. Watch the leash clip. When it droops, as in, gravity affects it, say "Good dog" and move forward. This will obviously take some time, and will take MORE time in the beginning. Your dog will learn to keep the leash loose in order to keep going forward. Don\'t pull your dog back, if they pull, but YOU set the length of the leash and keep it however you want it.')
B.Ut=s([B.P0,B.Oj,B.Pi],t.J)
B.NS=new A.dV("Loose leash walking","loose-leash","## Goal\n\nYour dog will walk next to you without pulling on the leash.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** be consistent in your training; it will greatly affect your dog's learning ability.\n- **DO** influence your dog's ability to stay near you because *you* are more exciting than the rest of the environment. *(Yes, this will take time. Rome wasn't built in a day, and neither is loose-leash walking.)*\n- **DON'T** yank on the leash, jerk it back, or always keep it tight because *you* are pulling *your dog*.\n\n> Note: Sometimes, if your dog has not learned to walk on a loose leash yet, you just need to make sure they do so. An example of this might be in the lobby at the vet's; outside the car at the dog park; through a crowd on the sidewalk. In Phase 1 you'll learn how to *prevent* your dog from pulling. In Phase 2 you'll learn to teach your dog where to walk, using rewards. In Phase 3 you'll learn to teach your dog where to walk *without* using food.\n",B.Ut,"https://youtu.be/7NrS6fWdqhE")
B.Vz=s([B.NV,B.NM,B.O5,B.NX,B.O0,B.NS],t.e7)
B.Py=new A.pf("Week 2",2,"Remember that you must treat **every time** you click or use your marker word in order to maintain its effectiveness. Continue to train in multiple SHORT sessions nearly every day and train in at least three different locations every week.",B.Vz,null)
B.OU=new A.aS("course-L1W3-stay-p1",'**Phase 1:** With your dog sitting at your left side, place your open hand in front of their nose for just a moment. Say "Stay," and step, *right foot first*, in front of your dog. If they get up, re-set them, and make it easier the next time by only moving your right foot a bit. Click or mark / feed if they stay seated. Do this 10x or until your dog stays seated 3x in a row.')
B.Pa=new A.aS("course-L1W3-stay-p2",'**Phase 2:** With your dog seated at your left side, say "Stay," and step, right foot first, *one step ahead of your dog*. Do this 10x or until your dog stays seated 3x in a row.')
B.Pe=new A.aS("course-L1W3-stay-p3","**Phase 3:** Continue this drill, and step in a different direction each time. Click or mark / feed as your dog stays seated.")
B.O9=new A.aS("course-L1W3-stay-p4","**Phase 4:** Repeat as above, but now add longer periods of time, adding 1\u20132 seconds at a time, until your dog will stay seated for 30 seconds.")
B.Wa=s([B.OU,B.Pa,B.Pe,B.O9],t.J)
B.NU=new A.dV("Stay","stay","## Goal\n\nWhen you say \"Stay,\" your dog will remain in its position until you say \"Okay.\"\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** keep this simple, with no longer than a 1\u20133 second stay to start, in a non-distracting area, when your dog is hungry.\n- **DO** use a hand signal *and* a verbal cue to start, but practice both separately eventually.\n- **DON'T** use a harsh tone, or stare at your dog or point or threaten them. When you teach it, they will do it.\n- **DON'T** experiment with seeing *if* your dog will stay unless they are in a safe location \u2014 don't see if they will run out the front door or your yard.\n",B.Wa,"https://youtu.be/Eo1VzYx-Wh4")
B.Xl=s([B.NU],t.e7)
B.Pv=new A.pf("Week 3",3,'*Tempting though it is\u2026 do not use your clicker or marker word to get your dog\'s attention. Ensure that every time your dog moves towards you (comes!), they have a wonderful experience.*\n\nThis week introduces the **"3 D\'s"** that you\'ll layer onto every behavior from now on:\n\n- **Distance** \u2014 How far away do you have to be when you ask your dog to sit / lie down / come?\n- **Distractions** \u2014 Can your dog do these behaviors in front of others? In front of other dogs? In lots of locations?\n- **Duration** \u2014 How long can your dog hold a sit or a down?\n\nA good rule of thumb: **When you increase one "D," decrease the other two.**\n\n> The original PDF includes a daily goals/results chart for tracking progress across all behaviors. A dedicated daily-goal tracker is coming in a future PuppyPath update; for now the phase checkboxes here capture per-behavior completion.\n',B.Xl,null)
B.OK=new A.aS("course-L1W4-leave-it-p1","**Phase 1:** With your dog on-leash, stand on the leash. Hold a low-value piece of food in your closed fist. Have a higher-value piece of food in a small bowl nearby. Present your fist to your dog. If they try to bite your fist, put it behind your back for two seconds, then re-present it. When your dog moves their nose away, lies down, or backs up, click or mark / feed, then give them the higher-value piece of food. Do this 10\u201320x, or until your dog reliably moves away from your fist when you hold it out.")
B.OT=new A.aS("course-L1W4-leave-it-p2","**Phase 2:** Present the lower-value item in your *open* palm. If your dog moves towards it, close your hand into a fist. Once your dog has backed off, open your hand again. If your dog stays away, click or mark / feed, and give them the higher-valued treat. Do this 10\u201320x, or until your dog reliably moves away from your open palm.")
B.Oa=new A.aS("course-L1W4-leave-it-p3","**Phase 3:** In this phase, you will gradually lower your open palm to the ground. You should also begin to practice in other rooms, different times of the day, and with other people around.")
B.P_=new A.aS("course-L1W4-leave-it-p4",'**Phase 4:** Place the low-value treat on the ground. Say **"Leave it."** Be ready to cover it with your hand or foot should your dog make a grab for it! As above, when your dog moves away from the treat, click or mark / feed and give them the higher-valued treat. *From now on, say "Leave it" when you want the dog to not touch the item in question.*')
B.P2=new A.aS("course-L1W4-leave-it-p5","**Phase 5: Outdoors!** Make a prediction about how your dog will do, and work at the level that is most likely to be performed correctly.")
B.OM=new A.aS("course-L1W4-leave-it-p6",'**Phase 6:** Change up the treats slightly. Use a *slightly* better "leave it" treat, but always make sure the "You can have THIS ONE" treat is better (in your dog\'s eyes).')
B.WY=s([B.OK,B.OT,B.Oa,B.P_,B.P2,B.OM],t.J)
B.NN=new A.dV("Leave it","leave-it",'## Goal\n\nWhen you say "Leave it" your dog will turn away from the item in question, and will not have access to that item, ever.\n\n## Do\'s and Don\'ts\n\n- **DO** make sure that what the dog *can\'t* have is never as good as what they *can* have when you begin to train this skill. For example, the "Leave it" item might be kibble, and the reinforcer for leaving it might be cheese. *(This assumes your dog prefers cheese to kibble, of course; review the Paired-Choice Preference Assessment for this exercise.)*\n- **DO** make sure to go back to the last successful phase if your dog is not progressing (getting it right 90% of the time).\n- **DON\'T** let your dog get the "Leave it" item! If they are able to grab it even 1 of 5 times, you are giving the message, *"Try and grab it!"* instead of *"You will get something better if you leave it alone!"*\n\n> Remember: **Distance \u2013 Distraction \u2013 Duration.** When you increase one, decrease the others.\n',B.WY,"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sBUVnL66-jY")
B.XE=s([B.NN],t.e7)
B.Pu=new A.pf("Week 4",4,"*It is imperative that you practice in new locations this week. Remember to make it easier for your dog by using better treats and easier commands when you introduce an exercise in a new location/environment.*",B.XE,null)
B.OB=new A.aS("course-L1W5-go-to-mat-p1",'**Phase 1:** Have 6\u201310 small treats in your RIGHT hand; have your dog on-leash with your clicker (if you are using one) in your LEFT hand. Place the mat on the floor. Take your treat hand and, hiding the treats, *point* to the mat in a sweeping motion so your dog follows the treat to the mat. When your dog is on the mat (all four feet), click or mark / feed three times in a row. Then, say "Okay!" and move away briskly to encourage your dog to move off of the mat.')
B.P1=new A.aS("course-L1W5-go-to-mat-p2","**Phase 2:** Same as above but alternate having food in your hand and having no food in your hand.")
B.Pp=new A.aS("course-L1W5-go-to-mat-p3","**Phase 3:** Decrease the use of food in your hand. Increase the number of seconds your dog is lying on the bed before you click/treat.")
B.OX=new A.aS("course-L1W5-go-to-mat-p4","**Phase 4:** Begin to take small steps in various directions as your dog lies on the bed, while increasing the number of seconds they lie there.")
B.P9=new A.aS("course-L1W5-go-to-mat-p5","*Remember: if your dog is not doing what you expect, return to a previous phase for at least one session.*")
B.Yt=s([B.OB,B.P1,B.Pp,B.OX,B.P9],t.J)
B.O1=new A.dV("Go to mat","go-to-mat",'## Goal\n\nWhen you say "Go to your mat," your dog will run to their mat and lie down/stay until you say "Okay!"\n',B.Yt,"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HveGG8EsR_A")
B.VA=s([B.O1],t.e7)
B.Px=new A.pf("Week 5",5,"## Do's and Don'ts\n\n- **DO** keep the mat you will work with out of sight until it's time to train.\n- **DON'T** practice when you can predict your dog is too revved up to lie down for a minute or two.\n- **DO** refer to previous homework sheets for practice sessions; *training a dog is like cleaning the house \u2014 there's always work to do!*\n",B.VA,null)
B.OZ=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-name-p1","**Phase 1:** Stand right behind your dog and call their name \u2014 did they turn and look at you?")
B.Oy=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-name-p2","**Phase 2:** Have someone squeak a toy. Call your dog's name \u2014 did they turn and look at you?")
B.Og=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-name-p3","**Phase 3:** *Think of other ways you can make the environment more distracting, and try again!*")
B.YT=s([B.OZ,B.Oy,B.Og],t.J)
B.NW=new A.dV("Name recognition \u2014 generalization check","gen-name","Have someone hold your dog's favorite toy or treat.",B.YT,null)
B.Oc=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-attention-p1","**Phase 1:** Stand on the sidewalk outside your house with your dog on a leash. How long does it take for your dog to look at you?")
B.Oq=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-attention-p2","**Phase 2:** How long do they keep looking at you for?")
B.P4=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-attention-p3","**Phase 3:** Do this exercise in different locations.")
B.Wc=s([B.Oc,B.Oq,B.P4],t.J)
B.O4=new A.dV("Attention \u2014 generalization check","gen-attention","",B.Wc,null)
B.Pq=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-hand-target-p1","**Phase 1:** 10 feet away, indoors.")
B.OA=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-hand-target-p2","**Phase 2:** 5 feet away, outdoors.")
B.OV=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-hand-target-p3","**Phase 3:** When there are other dogs around!")
B.Or=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-hand-target-p4","**Phase 4:** When someone else is eating near your dog.")
B.VR=s([B.Pq,B.OA,B.OV,B.Or],t.J)
B.NQ=new A.dV("Hand targeting \u2014 generalization check","gen-hand-target",'Stand varying distances and in different locations and hold out your hand for your dog to touch *(this is a great way to silently "call" your dog if you are on the phone)*:',B.VR,null)
B.OG=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-leave-it-p1","**Phase 1:** Your slippers.")
B.Oi=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-leave-it-p2","**Phase 2:** Undergarments!")
B.Pn=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-leave-it-p3","**Phase 3:** Ugg boots or any clothes with fluffy trim.")
B.Uz=s([B.OG,B.Oi,B.Pn],t.J)
B.NT=new A.dV("Leave it \u2014 generalization check","gen-leave-it","It's not all about the food! What else might you ask your dog to *leave*?",B.Uz,null)
B.P5=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-sit-down-p1","**Phase 1:** Walk around your dog?")
B.On=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-sit-down-p2","**Phase 2:** Step over your dog?")
B.Ox=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-sit-down-p3","**Phase 3:** Toss a toy near them?")
B.OR=new A.aS("course-L1W6-gen-sit-down-p4","**Phase 4:** *Note how long they hold, with what distractions, and in which environments.*")
